              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Quinn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this recipe, however I simply omit the mayo (I am not a fan). More tang and less calories. I also use granulated garlic and onion instead of the salted varieties. Add a little parsley and some green onion (scallion) for brightness.",
            "datePublished": "2017-10-15T13:37:57.927Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Linda Farrell"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This salad dressing is amazing. It tastes like a cross between 1000 island and french. I am very skeptical when a recipe calls for canned tomato soup because it always has a can taste. Made this yesterday as written except used just under 1/2 cup light \"real\" mayo. There is no fooling, this makes a lot of great dressing. Not too tangy and not too sweet!",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-10T12:48:01.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "kay S"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this dressing, but prefer it with amount of ketchup rather than the tomato soup. Equal amount ketchep, mayo and oil.",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-27T15:00:33.580Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
